Some of this "big data" stuff could be done relatively simply (from
the programmers point of view) with some flavours of PDP11 FORTRAN,
which had support for VIRTUAL arrays that didn't really fit in memory.
Even where it wasn't officially supported there was sometimes DECUS
code to do something equivalent. Iirc, it was done using on-disk data
structures rather than in-memory, so there would be a significant
speed penalty, even in comparison with the "twiddle the MMU" stuff.
But the user saw it as nice and simple.


