>> around 1 MB of arrays in extended memory via the MMU.  Somewhere in 
>> the DECUS
>> stuff, there is alternative code which can use on-disk data instead 
>> which is a reasonable fit
>> when the memory is used as a small disk drive.  Under RT-11, the VM: 
>> device handler
>> worked well to reduce and actual disk drive's relatively slow transfer 
>> rates.
> 
> I find that rather unlikely. The array indexing is still just done using 
> a 16-bit integer, which limits the size of a virtual array to 65536 
> elements. Even with INTEGER*4, that would only become 256K. 1M is just 
> not possible to address with virtual arrays in PDP-11 FORTRAN. Neither 
