You would want to implement the NFS server for RSX in exactly the same 
way, or it wouldn't be very useful. Atleast that is my opninion. Except 
that the server itself would need to do the deblocking, it's not done by 
the hardware.
But the NFS server would have to go through the normal F11ACP in RSX. 
meaning that you cannot access anything but 512 byte blocks. So the byte 
offsets and sizes that might show up in NFS requests cannot be mapped 
directly to disk operations anyway. So you would need to run through 
disk blocks. And if the file accessed over NFS is a variable record file 
with implicit CRLF, I believe the NFS server should present the file as 
a stream of the contents, with CRLF appended after each record, the 
record lengths and paddings be removed, and there you are. Full 
transformation required.

