As you see, it comes down to parts of the same problem as with NFS. It 
is simpler through, in that you are not expecting other programs to 
access it on the fly, or randomly, so there are some things you don't 
care about (such as seeking in the converted result).

>> The tar-file itself should (obviously) be transferred as a binary file, 
>> and will survive the trip just fine.
>> A tar extraction will probably create problems.
>> I believe ZIP might be better. There is ZIP for VMS, which seems to 
>> handle file attributes and other VMSism just fine, while still (I 
>> assume) be compatible with other ZIP implementations.
