> I know about VMS zip, but have never used it.  

Used it, and it works the way you would expect and want. Files get 
cipped/unzipped along with the VMS specific attributes.
I haven't checked what happens if you extract a ZIP-file created on some 
other OS though.

>>>> And this in turn is then translated into a File ID, which is a 48-bit 
>>>> number, consisting of 3 16-bit parts, which is what all file operations 
>>>> are using when doing file operations. The FileID is very similar to the 
