Anecdote:

We (Helsinki University of Technology) had an RP07 disk in our
DECSYSTEM-20. When the DEC retired, we had the RP07 connected to our VAX
11/750. This was a process itself as ecen DEC couldn't reformat the disk
pack for 512 byte blocks (DEC-20 had 576 byte block, if I remember
correctly). Well, finally the RP07 was VAX-compatible but there was no
boot ROM for it. We had to use TU58 for many months as the bootstrap
device, only for the first block of course.

Finally the new boot ROM arrived. It was a 18-pin (or 20-28 pin) DIP. It
was packed in a small plasric box (ca. 0.5" x 2" x 2") which was packed
in a cardboard box (2" x 6" x 10") which was inside a large box (10" x
15" x 15").


