>> On the PDP11 side, you cannot physically get a new interrupt before the
>> previous one have been handled. That is actually true of all CPUs I've
>> ever written software for. If that wasn't true, you would face a serious
>> hung CPU syndrome, since the fielded interrupt itself should not be
>> looping the CPU, but just cause the interrupt to be taken once, and then
>> dealt with. :-)
>>
>> So yes, you do need to do some serious buffering somewhere if you were
>> to do this.
>>
>>>> So no matter how high the speed of the serial line is, or how high the
>>>> speed of the mass storage at the other end is, you will not be able to
>>>> get that much speed on the PDP-11 side, and even so, it will consume
