There was a gent in Ohio that had a nearly working qbus scsi card.
It used common scsi silicon, and an embedded x86 processor.
The firmware used converted bits of the simh mscp code.  He ran out
of time, and the project stalled.  Something about family and school
obligations.  He had hoped to sell enough boards to recoup some of
his costs, then open source the design.

But the point is it can be done, and it's not beyond the combined
capabilities of this, or any of several other overlapping groups.

