It does look like nothing much changed. However...

"I removed the 2x 32MB and added 4x 32MB which I know they are working
because I used them in a good server."

They may work in an x86 server but memory extracted from a working
unspecified x86 server is not guaranteed to work in any given Alpha
system. You need memory which is compatible with the requirements of
that particular Alpha box. Memory type and speed and various other not-
usually-relevant-in-x86 things all matter. I don't have the full
details handy but one thing you could try is the "DEC compatible"
memory suppliers and work from their specs for memory compatible with
your PWS (assuming these details are still online).

All other suggestions gratefully received.


