There is certainly a current limitation on the VLC power supply. I
remember finding it wouldn't drive one particular (1GB?) DEC disk when
I tried to upgrade it, but it would drive another of the same GB. It's
too long ago to remember details -- the disk that didn't work was
about 1 inch thick; one half that physical size was OK if that gives
any clues. All that happened, though, was that the VLC wouldn't power
up, and there was no permanent damage.

Have you got anything heavy standing on top of the VLC? There was a
problem that this flexed the PCB and stopped it working, but again I
think it was permanent not off and on. There was an FCO that involved
a strategically-placed washer (so we called it the "washer bug") but I
never saw what the DEC field servant actually put where.

Chris


