They work very fine for executables. The binary file transports 
perfectly between Unix and Windows. It's the text files that causes issues.

But for RSX the problem is much worse, since RSX have a whole bunch of 
different file formats, and basically none of them match particularly 
well to Unix.
The two that do are fixed length binary files, and STREAM files. The 
latter are only understood by RMS, and not FCS though, which limits 
