directly between server and client.   Note the difference with 
z/OS (descendent from MVS and OS/360) where the record structure
actually exists on the disk hardware.  Among the features of the
IBM disk controller is a search for a record by key.  You can
specify a record (block) key and the disk hardware will search
(linearly) through the file until it finds the record (block)
with that key.  It made a lot of sense in S/360 days, but processors
speeds have increased much faster than disk speeds, and memory
sizes have also increased.  

That is the reason for the extra complication for the z/OS 
NFS server.  
 
