Yeah, chips could be a problem.  I may end out trying what I have in
mind using one of the paralel interfaces as hooking directly to the
QBUS may cost more than the whole project wold be worth.

For those who's curiosity has been piqued, I heve recently seen a few
examples of boards that interface IDE disks to the raw bus on a few
old microcomputers.  Very few parts required and the cost is minimal.
I got curious about trying it for the PDP-11 and maybe even the VAX.

On another note, I have also recently seen a system that uses a serial
connection to a PC or MAC as a disk interface.  Giving some thought to
that as well.  It will be slow, but when you come right down to it,
probably not much slower than an RD51.  :-)

And my most ambitious project (and the one I am least likely to find
enough time to do before retirement) is a board that can emulate an
ST-506 disk while utilizing something icheaper and easier to find.

Anybody with ideas, feel free to jump in/

