IDE allowed for either 8 or 16 bit transfers, the 8 bit ability
disappeared pretty fast.  For Qbus presumably you won't have
that problem.

Also note that one of the modes of CF (compact flash) is a direct
emulation of IDE, though with 8 bit mode.  For most 8 bit 
microcomputers, the current size of CF cards is plenty big enough.

