What are the typical problems with the transceivers?  The one's I'm
using in my board are the 74AS641 (for the big bidirectional groups
like DAL) and
74AS757 (for the single bidirectional lines like RPLY or DIN/DOUT).
They're still generally available from Mouser and Digikey (though
sometimes not in big quantities) and they're compliant, for the most
part; I keep seeing people trying to use '245s, which are not open
collector or high-current, and I am continually puzzled by that.

The only thing I can see that's wrong with most of the things out
there is that they have a fast slew rate, which can be bad news bears
on a long backplane.  I'm not quite sure how much that'll kill things
in practice, though.  They're also not designed for a 1.5v threshold,
but I believe they should work on systems without too much ringing; I
suppose I'll have to see how my board does in practice.


- Dave


