OK, thanks.

Earlier I wrote that the mini-debugger talks to "the usual console"
and suggested verifying with the mini-debugger manual. What I meant
was that the mini-debugger talks (iirc) to the usual serial console.

In order to ensure that it tries the serial rather than graphics
console, remove any kbd and mouse (and maybe even the graphics card
too :)). Reducing the system to a minimum number of cards is often a
good step anyway in cases like this. Apologies if you already did
this.

Another manual, one which might even be relevant (though I haven't
really checked) is the "Troubleshooting the Digital Personal
Workstation" 'manual'. It's a web-based thing, and you can find one at
e.g.
http://www.turquoisewitch.com/~bradh/miata/Service/
