an IDE disk at one end, and an RQDX on the other end???

If so, then I can understand the comment about making it look like an RD54.

However, in this case I totally fail to see the point of talking about 
"Qbus", since it is not a Qbus controller at all. You might want to put 
it on the Qbus just to draw power, but that's it. You definitely don't 
need to worry about any Qbus interface chips at all.

But I know that I would never want to go down this path unless I was 
very desperate. The RQDX controllers are slow as molass. Not the thing I 
would want to keep in the loop anywhere.

